MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The lag bolts and fender washers fit my repeated purchases of fastener assortments: they add useful attachment options and complement hardware I already use.",
    "The threaded magnets, construction adhesive, and heat shrink tubing fit my interest in mounting, bonding, and protecting parts during repairs, with usefulness across several possible projects."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The bulkhead fitting and pressure gauge require a particular plumbing setup, thread size, or pressure range; my tool purchases do not establish that I have that application.",
    "The test leads and masks do not meet an immediate need for me. The alcohol is relevant to adhesive preparation, but I would need to confirm that 70% is suitable before choosing it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying workshop tools seems to have been treated as a reason to want specialized supplies for almost any repair task.",
    "A broad connection to measuring or adhesive work seems to have counted too much without checking whether the specific function or formulation fits my needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of bolts, rivets, rivet nuts, and other fasteners suggest that complementary mounting hardware is especially relevant right now.",
    "I can see a use for versatile supplies across projects, while specialized fittings and instruments need a concrete application and compatible specifications. Frequent shopping does not mean I need every adjacent tool."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my ongoing fastening and repair interests, but sometimes stretched those interests into specialized tasks I have not shown a need for."
}
